kosha reaction

  -- a chemical reaction: reactants → products with bond breaking and forming.
  -- the fundamental act of chemistry — the sandhi that produces something new.
  --
  -- what is conserved: atoms (mass). charge. energy (first law).
  -- what changes: bonds, molecular structure, energy distribution.
  --
  -- four measures of a reaction:
  --   enthalpy ΔH:   heat released (exothermic, ΔH<0) or absorbed (endothermic, ΔH>0)
  --   entropy ΔS:    change in disorder — gases have high entropy
  --   Gibbs ΔG:      ΔH - TΔS. ΔG<0 → spontaneous. the combined criterion.
  --   rate k:        how fast. activation energy Ea. catalyst lowers Ea.
  --
  -- reaction types:
  --   synthesis:       A + B → AB
  --   decomposition:   AB → A + B
  --   single replacement: A + BC → AC + B
  --   double replacement: AB + CD → AD + CB
  --   combustion:      fuel + O2 → CO2 + H2O + heat
  --   acid-base:       H⁺ donor + H⁺ acceptor → salt + water
  --   oxidation-reduction (redox): electron transfer between species
  --
  -- equilibrium: most reactions are reversible. at equilibrium, forward rate = reverse rate.
  -- K = [products]/[reactants] (equilibrium constant). K>>1 favours products.
  -- Le Chatelier: a system at equilibrium responds to stress by minimising it.

